//fldigi macro definition file extended
// =============================================================================
// Author: Brian McLaughlin (N3BMC)
// Creation Date: 2026-08-25
// Description: Routine RTTY QSO Macros
//
// Revision History:
// Date       Init  Description
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2026-08-25 BMC   Header added to older file
// 2026-09-23 BMC   Fixed major problem that has been plaguing me! Macros don't
//                  like an <IDLE:n> tag if you don't have a <TX> as well. I
//                  was adding <IDLE:n> with some of my end macros to keep the
//                  modem sync up. Bad idea! Fixed and now FSK is working great
//                  for me too.
// =============================================================================

// Row 1 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Macro # 1
/$ 0 CQ@#-2+
<TX><IDLE:1>
CQ CQ CQ DE <MYCALL> <MYCALL> PSE K\n
<RX><AFTER:20>


//
// Macro # 2
/$ 1 ANS @>|
<TX><IDLE:1>
<CALL> <CALL> de <MYCALL> <MYCALL> KN\n
<RX>


//
// Macro # 3
/$ 2 QSO @>>
<TX><IDLE:1>
<CALL> DE <MYCALL> 


//
// Macro # 4
/$ 3 KN @|| 
<CALL> DE <MYCALL> KN
<RX>


//
// Macro # 5
/$ 4 SK @|| 
TNX FOR QSO 73 73  <CALL> DE <MYCALL> SK   \n
<RX>


//
// Macro # 6
/$ 5 Me/Qth 
<MYNAME> <MYQTH> <MYST> <MYLOC> \n


//
// Macro # 7
/$ 6 Brag
RUNNING AN IC-7300 AT <TX_PWR>W ON A <ANTENNA> /W FLDIGI ON A MAC MINI\n


//
// Macro # 8
/$ 7 AGN? @>|
<TX><IDLE:1>
AGN? AGN?\n
<RX>


//
// Macro # 9
/$ 8 


//
// Macro # 10
/$ 9 


//
// Macro # 11
/$ 10 Tx @>>
<TX><IDLE:1>


//
// Macro # 12
/$ 11 Rx @||
<RX>


